{{!--
  GoatCounter page-view counting. mdBook appends this file to the <head> of
  every page, so each page load counts once under its own path; the dashboard
  sums those into the site totals.

  The path is normalized so one page always lands on one row:
  - The query string is dropped. Search results link to pages with
    ?highlight=<term>, which would otherwise split a page across a row per
    search term.
  - The .html extension is dropped. GitHub Pages serves /guide/trading and
    /guide/trading.html as the same page, so counting both forms separately
    would split it.
  - A trailing index collapses to its directory, so / and /index.html count
    as one page.

  GitHub Pages serves 404.html at the missing URL, so a broken link counts
  under that URL with the title "Page not found", which makes dead inbound
  links visible on the dashboard.

  The settings object must exist before count.js loads, which is why it sits
  in its own script tag above the async loader. GoatCounter skips localhost by
  default, so `mdbook serve` previews are not counted.
--}}
<script>
    window.goatcounter = {
        path: function () {
            return location.pathname.replace(/\.html$/, '').replace(/\/index$/, '/');
        }
    };
</script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://bazaardocs.goatcounter.com/count"
        async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
